    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="1288" n="1276" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg1276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.4016/9–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the United States Political Adviser for Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Berlin</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-14T20:00:00-04:00">September 14,
                            1945—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>479. Lane has been authorized to approach PolGov on suspension of expulsions of
                    Germans as requested in your 509, September 11.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d613-f1"/>
                    Latest data available here indicates approximately four and half million persons
                    have entered Soviet zone from areas east of Oder and Neisse.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d613-f1" n="99" xml:id="d613-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 91, <ref target="#pg1274">p. 1274</ref>. The authorization to the
                    Ambassador in Poland was contained in telegram 103, September 14, 8 p.m.
                    (840.4016/9–1445).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
